{
  "dom_id": "step-103219",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Solving Equations Using Cross Multiplication",
  "problem": "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{1}{3} = -\\dfrac{ax}{5}$ for the variable $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =-\\frac{ax}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{-ax}{5} \\\\ 5\\cdot 1 & =3\\cdot (-ax) \\\\ 5 & =-3ax\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3a\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =-3ax \\\\ \\frac{5}{-3a} & =\\frac{-3ax}{-3a} \\\\ \\frac{5}{-3a} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-3a}x}{\\cancel{-3a}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3a} & =x \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{3a}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
